=== PARITY (vs web CommandHistoryWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (CommandHistorySource -> CommandHistoryModel):
    useCommandHistory, useVehicles, useTranslation, useCommands. The production app wires
    CommandHistorySource over the KMP command-history StateHolderModel<...> (fed by useCommandHistory +
    the useVehicles vehicle pick); the view performs NO HTTP. No direct transport in the view.
  Projection -> CommandHistoryBuilder is a 1:1 port of the web feedItems memo + formatCommandName +
    STATUS_MAP + WidgetEventFeed:
      formatCommandName: replace '_'->' ' then upper-case each word-initial char (port of
        replace(/\b\w/g, c => c.toUpperCase()); the rest of each word is preserved, e.g. HORN_honk -> "HORN Honk").
      status(fromRaw:): exact-key STATUS_MAP lookup on the lower-cased Tesla command-log values
        (success/failed/pending), anything else -> .other (web DEFAULT_STATUS). Case-sensitive like web.
      makeEntry fallbacks: commandName = formatCommandName(command ?? '—'); rawStatus = status ?? '—';
        timestamp = created_at ?? epoch.
      feedEntries newest-first + cap 10 (web WidgetEventFeed sort+slice maxItems=10); latestEntry = list[0]
        (input order); relativeTime buckets (<1m justNow / <60m minutes / <24h hours / else absolute).
    Verified by an EXECUTED harness (31/31, below) — real cached->projection, not a typecheck.
  Composition -> WidgetShell chrome (terminal SF Symbol + "Command History" title + freshness chip + refresh
    + optional Open) · COMPACT (cols<=1): terminal glyph + humanized command name + status Badge
    (success->Success/.success, failed->Failed/.danger, else->Pending/.warning — faithful port of the web
    CompactView ternaries) over a 44pt min-height, or the inline empty row · FEED (cols>=2): scrollable
    timeline of rows (status-tinted marker [check/green, xmark/red, clock/amber, terminal/gray] + connector,
    humanized command name, raw status subtitle, relative time). Recharts->none / Leaflet->none (no chart/map).
  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton rows) · empty ("No commands sent", ContentUnavailableView) ·
    error (retry) · stale (chip + banner over cached feed) · offline (cached feed + chip + banner) ·
    content. Model phase resolution keeps cached rows visible behind refresh/errors, matching the web
    shell (skeleton only on initial fetch; empty only when there are no commands).
  i18n -> all 5 web source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback:
    widget.commandHistory ("Command History"), widget.commandSuccess ("Success"),
    widget.commandFailed ("Failed"), widget.commandPending ("Pending"), widget.noCommands
    ("No commands sent") -> ALL PRESENT in CommandHistoryWidget.strings. The web's hardcoded relative-time
    English literals ("Just now", "{m}m ago", "{h}h ago") are promoted to catalog keys
    (widget.command.justNow/minutesAgo/hoursAgo) so NO English literal lives in native code.
  a11y -> each feed/compact row is one VoiceOver element with a localized composed label
    (CommandHistoryAccessibility.rowLabel: command name, status, relative time); every header button
    (refresh / open) has an accessibilityLabel; the timeline rail + status icons are accessibilityHidden;
    Dynamic Type via Font.TS tokens; Reduce Motion respected by the shared TSSkeleton.
  Telemetry -> CommandHistoryModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"CommandHistoryWidget") ->
    bridges shared Telemetry.track(.screenView) (P1/S11). Asserted by a spy test.
  Registry -> CommandHistoryWidget.registration: id "command-history", category "commands", default 2x4,
    min 1x2, max 4x40 (+ clamp()), matching registry/commands.ts. Asserted.

